            <ArticleTitle>Is hyperinsulinemia required to develop overeating-induced obesity?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>691-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2012.11.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(12)00462-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Type 2 diabetes is characterized by insulin resistance, and the hyperinsulinemia commonly observed in patients is thought to be a compensatory response. Yet it has been difficult to disentangle cause and effect. Mehran et al. (2012) provide genetic evidence that a reduction of insulin secretion prevents high-fat feeding-induced obesity.</AbstractText>
